@startuml mvp_session_state
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
title MVP session and error transitions — owner decisions through 19 October
[*] --> Boot
Boot --> Idle : software-observable startup checks pass
Boot --> Muted : non-Wi-Fi startup check fails / Error, mute
Idle --> Listening : Start / Heart or Lung
Idle --> Portal : long press >= 2 s, or automatically when no Wi-Fi credentials are stored / Idle network lease, scan then open hotspot
Portal --> Idle : verified join + save (or save warning) / 10 s result, close AP/server, retain station
Portal --> Idle : cancel or inactivity / notice, teardown, retain station if connected
Portal --> Listening : Start / safe setup teardown first; retain established station
Listening --> Measuring : Heart session begins / freeze context
Listening --> Muted : catalogue halting fault / mute
Measuring --> Muted : catalogue halting fault / mute, invalidate
Listening --> Idle : Stop in Lung / mute, no BPM or send
Measuring --> Idle : Stop before 15 s / cancel, no send
Measuring --> Analysing : Stop at or after 15 s / mute, finalize
Analysing --> Sending : valid BPM + configured prerequisites
Analysing --> ReportingError : invalid BPM + validated error contract + prerequisites
Analysing --> Idle : Wi-Fi unconfigured / no send or Wi-Fi error
Analysing --> Idle : delivery prerequisites fail / latch DELIVERY_NOT_POSSIBLE
Sending --> Idle : receipt 201 / 200
Sending --> Idle : failed after 3 retries / latch DELIVERY_FAILURE
ReportingError --> Idle : error report received / no numeric BPM
ReportingError --> Idle : report failed after 3 retries / latch DELIVERY_FAILURE
note as NormalFaultIndication
  Error latch (red LED) is independent of workflow state.
  Several errors: LEDs show the highest priority, then the first latched.
  Short press acknowledges where catalogue permits; no implicit retry.
  Wi-Fi recovery does not require acknowledgement.
  Preserve the current workflow; no implicit Start.
end note
Muted --> Boot : restart required [catalogue]
Muted --> Idle : short press [catalogue permits acknowledgement]
note right of Analysing
  Start = Busy, visible activity.
  No cancellation or queued Start.
end note
note right of Sending
  Same Busy rule during both send paths.
  Exclusive network lease; audio stopped.
end note
note bottom of Measuring
  Reject mode/context changes with SESSION_CONTEXT_CHANGE; halt/restart per catalogue.
  Never apply the rejected identity; invalidate halted acquisition.
  Wi-Fi-only faults preserve functioning audio.
  Other faults follow catalogue halt/clear rules.
  Normal-fault indication is latched separately from workflow;
  acknowledgement does not change an active workflow.
end note
note bottom of Muted
  Non-Wi-Fi faults halt according to current catalogue (19 October).
  Mute; invalidate incomplete work; block Start.
  Restart-required faults cannot be cleared by short press.
end note
@enduml
